{"question_id":"Q001","question":"How many remote days per week are allowed today, and is a change already announced?","snapshot_at":"2026-06-20T23:59:59Z","asked_at":"2026-06-20T23:59:59Z","answer":"{\n  \"answer\": \"A change has been announced regarding the number of remote working days per week.\",\n  \"cited_clauses\": [\"D101#C1\", \"D103#C1\", \"D104#C1\"],\n  \"reasoning\": \"The current policy allows permanent employees to work remotely for a maximum of two days per week as stated in clause D101#C1. However, the most recent policies allow up to four remote days per week starting on 1 July 2026, as mentioned in clauses D103#C1 and D","cited_clauses":["D103#C1","D102#C1"],"retrieved_chunks":[{"clause_id":"D103#C1","document_id":"D103","score":0.6843425324469826,"text":"From 1 July 2026, permanent employees may work remotely for a maximum of four days per week.","metadata":{"document_id":"D103","policy_family":"remote_work","version":"3.0","publication_date":"2026-06-15","effective_from":"2026-07-01","effective_to":null,"department":"HR","issuer":"HR Director","approval_status":"approved","source_class":"corporate_policy","locations":["Pune","Mumbai"],"employee_category":"permanent","conditions":[]}},{"clause_id":"D102#C1","document_id":"D102","score":0.6787684408115237,"text":"From 1 February 2026, permanent employees may work remotely for a maximum of three days per week.","metadata":{"document_id":"D102","policy_family":"remote_work","version":"2.0","publication_date":"2026-01-15","effective_from":"2026-02-01","effective_to":null,"department":"HR","issuer":"HR Director","approval_status":"approved","source_class":"corporate_policy","locations":["Pune","Mumbai"],"employee_category":"permanent","conditions":[]}},{"clause_id":"D104#C1","document_id":"D104","score":0.6660305910888616,"text":"Permanent staff in Pune and Mumbai can use up to four remote-working days each week from 1 July 2026.","metadata":{"document_id":"D104","policy_family":"remote_work","versi